extends RefCounted
# Factual account-feature notices prepared for review. No consent is auto-recorded.
const PRIVACY := "Adventure Odyssey account data notice\nDraft for developer review | October 19, 2026\n\nEmail accounts\nWhen you choose Create Account or Sign In, the app sends your email address and password over HTTPS to Google Firebase Authentication for the Adventure Odyssey project. Firebase handles account registration and authentication. Verification and password-reset requests ask Firebase to send an email to the address you enter. Network requests also disclose connection information such as your IP address to the service.\n\nOn this device\nThe app does not save your password to a file or include it in application logs. By default, signed-in account identifiers and session tokens are held in memory for the current app session, and restarting requires signing in again. Optional Remember me is off by default. On supported Android devices, choosing it stores only a refresh token and its account/project identifiers in authenticated encrypted storage protected by Android Keystore, outside Android backup storage. It does not save your password or ID token. Restoring a saved login requires an online check with Firebase. Signing out removes the saved login; if removal fails, the app warns you to retry before sharing the device. You can remove a saved login from the sign-in screen. Keystore protection depends on the device; hardware-backed protection is not promised. Clearing form fields is not a guarantee of forensic erasure from device memory or third-party keyboards.\n\nYour adventure\nCharacter appearance, inventory, equipment, quests, gold, Sigils and other progress remain in the existing local save on this device. Signing in does not upload that save, create a cloud backup, merge characters or transfer ownership of the guest character. Guest play remains available offline. Uninstalling or losing the device can lose local progress.\n\nOther services\nThis account client does not add advertising, analytics, purchases, SMS sign-in or location collection. Google sign-in is not yet implemented in the app. Google processes information under its service policies; see https://policies.google.com/privacy and https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy for provider information. Your operating system, keyboard and download platform have their own policies.\n\nQuestions and account requests\nDeveloper/support: Dabsky, dabskycreativestudio@gmail.com. You may contact this address about the account record or request account deletion. Do not email a password or session token. Emailing support shares your email and message with that mailbox. Deleting an online account and deleting a local adventure are separate actions; logging out does neither.\n\nReview status\nThis notice describes the implemented client behavior. The developer must review the operator details, audience requirements, provider settings and account-request procedures before enabling public account registration. This draft does not claim legal compliance or promise a particular provider retention period."
const TERMS := "Adventure Odyssey account preview information\nDraft for developer review | October 19, 2026\n\nThis unfinished game provides a local guest adventure and a developing optional email-account feature. Account services require connectivity and may be unavailable or rate-limited. The current account feature does not provide cloud saves, multiplayer, purchases or a server-authoritative currency balance.\n\nUse an email address you control and a unique password. Do not share passwords or session tokens. Verification and recovery links are handled by the account provider. Signing in does not change the ownership or storage of your existing local character. Update the app without uninstalling to retain compatible local saves; no cloud recovery is currently provided.\n\nThe accompanying account data notice explains what is sent to Firebase and what remains on the device. Reading these draft documents does not create an account or record agreement. An account is requested only when you submit the Create Account form.\n\nThese are preview feature notes, not final adopted terms. They do not waive consumer rights, impose arbitration, select a court or set a liability cap. The developer must review any final agreement and required disclosures before an online public release. Support: dabskycreativestudio@gmail.com."
